{
  "_comment": [
    "Vanilla (1.21.90+) ships its own per-biome Vibrant Visuals settings, and those",
    "take precedence over any global lighting/color_grading JSON a custom pack provides.",
    "To make this pack actually apply in vanilla worlds we emit one client biome file",
    "per biome that points at our own lighting / color grading identifiers.",
    "Nether and End biomes are intentionally left untouched so they keep their vanilla look.",
    "Profile keys map to lighting/<profile>.json + color_grading/<profile>.json.",
    "Water is a single shared configuration: Vibrant Visuals cannot blend the waves on/off flag or caustics between biomes, so every biome points at the same one.",
    "The 'default' profile lives in lighting/global.json + color_grading/color_grading.json.",
    "Only biome IDs that exist in the shipping game are listed: an unknown ID makes the client log 'Loaded client biome but no biome with that name exists'."
  ],
  "profiles": {
    "default": {
      "lighting_identifier": "kage:default_lighting",
      "color_grading_identifier": "kage:default_color_grading",
      "atmosphere_identifier": "kage:default_atmospherics",
